WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.095 --> 00:00:02.380
(gentle music)

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.680
- [Narrator] Satellite images show

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.750
a buildup of Russian military activity

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.120
at the Ukrainian border in recent weeks.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.440
- There is concern that Russia is actually

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.650
getting ready to invade
its smaller neighbor.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.483
The Kremlin denies this.

00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:20.130
(Lavrov speaking in foreign language)

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.640
- [Narrator] But US intelligence revealed

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.140
that Moscow has drawn up plans

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.930
for a military invasion of Ukraine

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.980
that could involve around 175,000 troops

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.583
as soon as next year.

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:32.250
- In the meeting with Putin
I was very straightforward.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.230
If in fact he invades Ukraine,

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:38.083
there'll be severe consequences.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.280
- [Narrator] Ukraine
has been trying to join

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.130
Western organizations
like NATO and the EU,

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.720
but this is at odds
with what Russia wants,

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.630
which is to have influence
over the country.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.070
The US and Russia have recently

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.160
expelled diplomats over cybercrime

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.910
and clashed over energy supplies

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.420
and a migrant crisis on the border

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.420
between Belarus and Poland.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.050
- After the summit between President Biden

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.180
and President Putin in June,

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.060
there was a glimmer of
hope that the countries

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.470
might set a different course,

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.670
but again there has been this struggle.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.630
- [Narrator] Here's how the clash

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.570
between the US and Russia over Ukraine

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:16.213
is worsening an already
tense relationship.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:19.550
Russia invaded Ukraine

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.990
and seized the Ukrainian
peninsula of Crimea

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:25.633
after the country staged a
pro-Western revolution in 2014.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.930
Ever since then, Russian
President Vladimir Putin

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:32.900
has tried to prevent Ukraine's
drift towards the West.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.600
Ukraine has for a long
time wanted to join NATO

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.260
and Putin has voiced anger
of the US and its allies'

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.440
financial and military
support of the country.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.990
- The Kremlin has made very clear

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:48.170
that they feel that any kind
of deployment of NATO troops

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.560
in Eastern Ukraine,

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.250
which would be Russia's western borders,

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.640
would be a threat.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.676
And for Russia that is a red light.

00:01:56.676 --> 00:02:01.093
(Putin speaking in foreign language)

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.550
- [Ann] The key question would be,

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.910
specially in relation to the
Russian buildup of troops

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.370
on the border,

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:14.480
how far would the US and
NATO be willing to go

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.350
in order to protect Ukraine?

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.550
- [Narrator] While the US and NATO

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.610
have no obligation to help Ukraine,

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.230
the Biden administration has threatened

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.120
serious sanctions against Russia

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.120
and said it wouldn't
tolerate another invasion

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.170
like the one in 2014.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.260
Washington has also said

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:31.400
it would help protect
Ukraine's sovereignty

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.543
but pressed Kiev to reform
internal issues like corruption.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.420
Tensions between Russia and the US

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.440
have been building for a while.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.150
The US recently imposed sanctions

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:44.270
and ordered the expulsion of
more than 50 Russian diplomats

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:45.700
by June 30th

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.670
based on allegations of cyberattacks

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.930
and US election interference.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.900
Moscow retaliated by doing the same,

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.580
ordering the removal of
several US embassy personnel

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:55.763
from Russia by next year.

00:02:55.763 --> 00:02:58.160
- This is the kind of of tit for tat,

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.290
what they call mirror
measures taken against the US

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:07.290
who they say has basically
violated diplomatic norms.

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:10.060
So there is definitely
this back and forth,

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:13.150
this diplomatic tug of war, if you wish.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:14.840
- [Narrator] In a call
with Putin in December,

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.900
Biden warned that if Russia
made any moves in Ukraine,

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.040
the US would prevent the
completion of Russia's

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.570
Nord Stream 2 pipeline

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.060
which Washington sees as a threat

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.300
to European energy independence.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.110
The pipeline would transport natural gas

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.220
from Russia to Europe

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:31.113
and be a huge source of
energy revenue for Moscow.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.870
Russia is a major
exporter of gas to Europe

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:38.000
and an important channel
runs through Belarus.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.050
Belarusian President Alexander Lukashenko

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.650
recently threatened to
disrupt that flow of energy

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.930
after the EU imposed
sanctions on the country

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.680
over a migrant crisis in November

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.601
on its border with Poland.

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:53.434
(Lukashenko speaking in foreign language)

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.640
- [Narrator] Western
leaders have accused Russia

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.730
of helping exacerbate the crisis,

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.403
a claim that Moscow denies.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.980
Earlier on in Biden's presidency,

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.630
Washington had wanted to establish

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.820
a closer relationship with the Kremlin,

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:11.280
but as tensions escalate over Ukraine,

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.220
political analysts say the two
aren't making much progress

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.290
towards that goal.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:17.000
- A lot of it can boil down to the fact

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.110
that actually feels that
it has been ignored.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.440
Both countries have said

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.810
of course we do not
want this confrontation,

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.720
but it seems as though a lot of the times

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.360
it's one step forward, two steps back

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:32.680
as they each try to maintain influence

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.640
and not want to be seen as the weaker

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.025
between the two sides.

00:04:38.025 --> 00:04:40.692
(gentle music)

